{"name":"Ecru White","hex":"#d6d1c0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ecru","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A beige colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a beige colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ecru"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ecru","blocks":[{"text":"Ecru is a grayish yellow or cream colour. It initially indicated the colour of unbleached linen, and some English dictionaries still define it this way. However, over the years, it has also come to be used for a much darker color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/LeicesterFronteiriza.jpg/330px-LeicesterFronteiriza.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ecru"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White"}],"images":[{"srcset"